# 11. PHASE H — CHATBOT AND ANALYTICAL PLATFORM DESIGN

Design the future solution with:

### Data layer

Approved local Parquet files and DuckDB.

### Mapping layer

A versioned, evidence-based Scenario Manager-to-HDS factor registry.

### Quantitative engine

Deterministic Python functions performing all calculations.

### LLM layer

An approved enterprise LLM that translates natural-language questions into validated structured requests.

### API layer

FastAPI with approved calculation endpoints.

### User interface

A professional analytical workspace with:

- Chatbot
- Factor search
- Historical time-series charts
- Rolling-shock distribution
- Percentile tables
- Historical extreme events
- Scenario Manager comparisons
- Mapping evidence
- Data quality and freshness
- Export to Excel

### Governance

- Approved user authentication
- Read-only data access by default
- Audit trails
- Model and methodology versioning
- Source lineage
- Mapping approval
- Analyst review
- No arbitrary LLM-generated SQL
- No automatic production scenario updates

Investigate suitable enterprise deployment options, including local prototype and approved internal shared hosting.

Do not assume a personal workstation is suitable as the permanent production server.

